 "Player": "Jugador",
 "Survival": "Supervivencia",
 "Health": "Salud",
 "Live from the player object.": "",
 "Infinite Health": "Salud infinita",
 "Talion takes no damage: the game's damage code writes your max health instead of the lowered value (enemies and allies are hit normally). A 10x-a-second refill stays on as a backup.": "",
 "No Summon Cooldown": "Invocar sin espera",
 "Summon followers / bodyguards and call mounts again right away. Applies to the next summon (a cooldown already running finishes normally).": "",
 "Heal Now": "Curar ahora",
 "Heal": "Curar",
 "Power": "Poder",
 "Infinite Focus": "Concentración infinita",
 "The game's own developer switch for Focus (bow slow-motion).": "",
 "Infinite Might": "Poderío infinito",
 "The game's own developer switch for Might (executions, combos).": "",
 "Might Never Drains (no full-Might sound)": "El poderío nunca baja (sin sonido)",
 "Might stays full: attacks no longer spend it, so it never refills - which removes the growl/chime the game plays every time Might fills back up (that sound came from Infinite Might refilling). One-byte patch in the game's Might setter. Use it instead of, or together with, Infinite Might.": "",
 "Infinite Elf Shot": "Disparos élficos infinitos",
 "The game's own developer switch for Elf-Shot.": "",
 "Infinite Elven Rage": "Furia élfica infinita",
 "The game's own developer switch for Wrath / Elven Rage.": "",
 "Elven Rage Refills After Use": "La furia élfica se recarga al usarla",
 "Elven Rage runs its normal length (the Wrath meter drains), then the meter fills up again as soon as rage ends, ready for the next one. Use this INSTEAD of Infinite Elven Rage (keep that one off - it keeps rage on until you switch it off).": "",
 "Arrows": "Flechas",
 "Wraith Chain": "Cadena espectral",
 "Chain Without Aiming": "Encadenar sin apuntar",
 "Chain targets are picked all around you (360 degrees, up to 25 m, closest first), not only where the camera faces. Also widens normal melee targeting, which the chain uses. The game reads these rules once when it starts, so after turning this ON, restart the game for it to take effect.": "",
 "No Chain Slow-Motion": "Cadena sin cámara lenta",
 "Celebrimbor's chain runs at full speed: the world and the spirit are no longer slowed while he jumps from orc to orc, and stealth / execution kills lose their slow-motion. Talion still holds still while the spirit chains, as the game intends.": "",
 "Fast Chain": "Cadena rápida",
 "The camera fly to the next target is 4x quicker. With No Chain Slow-Motion on, the whole chain plays at full speed.": "",
 "Skills": "Habilidades",
 "Progression": "Progreso",
 "Level": "Nivel",
 "Talion's level through the game's own level setter (level-up rewards included; capped at the game's table, 80).": "",
 "Skill Points": "Puntos de habilidad",
 "Live count through the game's inventory. Type a number to set it; L = keep it there (infinite skill points).": "",
 "Add 10 Skill Points": "Añadir 10 puntos de habilidad",
 "Mirian": "",
 "Live count through the game's inventory. Type a number to set it; L = keep it there (infinite Mirian).": "",
 "Add 100,000 Mirian": "Añadir 100.000 mirian",
 "Items": "Objetos",
 "Give Item": "Dar objeto",
 "Any of the game's 5618 item records by exact name, e.g. Gem_Blade_5Wondrous, Runegem_Red_Dmg_5Wondrous, Runegem_Green_Health_5Wondrous, Runegem_White_Resource_5Wondrous, XP_Boost, SkillPoint. Full list: research\\db\\Inventory_Items.txt": "",
 "Skill Tree": "Árbol de habilidades",
 "Choose Multiple Skills": "Elegir varias habilidades",
 "Activating an upgrade no longer switches the other upgrades of that skill off (one-byte patch in the game's skill switcher). Keep this ON while you use the upgrade buttons below and when you activate upgrades in the game's skill menu.": "",
 "Upgrades Work Together (Shadow Dominate fix)": "Las mejoras funcionan juntas",
 "With every upgrade active, some upgrades block each other. Fixed so far: Shadow Dominate did nothing because owning the Shadow Pull upgrade switched off its dash-to-target moves. Only Dominate's own check is removed; Shadow Strike and Shadow Strike Kill keep their normal tap/hold behaviour. In-memory game data, re-applied after every launch.": "",
 "Unlock All Skills in the Menu": "Desbloquear todas en el menú",
 "The skill menu lets you buy every skill now: story-locked ones ('Unlocked by playing Story Quests'), ones above your level and ones missing prerequisites. You buy them with skill points and the game grants them its own way. From the 'Unlock All Skills' CT.": "",
 "Activate All Upgrades": "Activar todas las mejoras",
 "Every Talion skill and upgrade in the skill menu, owned and active at the same time, including the story-unlocked ones (Shadow Strider, Dominate, Death Threat ...) and the 6 Prestige skills (set their ranks below). Gives the game's own skill items; no story or quest flags are touched. Skips cut content the game never finished. Needs Choose Multiple Skills ON. Some upgrades are alternative versions of one move - the game still plays one of them per use.": "",
 "ALL": "TODAS",
 "Re-activate Swapped Upgrades": "Reactivar mejoras cambiadas",
 "Turns back on every upgrade you already bought that was switched off earlier (buys nothing). Needs Choose Multiple Skills ON.": "",
 "RESTORE": "RESTAURAR",
 "Raise the Dead (Dark Talion) - see warning": "Alzar a los muertos (Talion oscuro) - ver aviso",
 "The end-game Raise Dead skill now, without finishing the story. Puts Raise Dead + its 3 upgrades (Undying Loyalty, Death Troll, Undying Beast) in the Story row of the skill menu, gives the skill items, and turns on the game's own Dark Talion state that the ability needs (Raise Dead does not fire without it, even with the attack gates opened). Raises everything: grunts, Ologs, sappers, enemy AND your captains (as followers), every creature (caragors, graugs, spiders, fell beasts...), up to 30 per kind per cast, decapitated bodies too (heads still fly off; beheaded captains can come back in the Nemesis system). Use: fill Might, then press [T] near fallen enemies. Isildur's Ring (Raise Dead radius) now works too. Story progress is not changed. Re-applied after every load. WARNING: Raise Dead only works in the game's own Dark Talion state, so this toggle turns it on. Dark Talion changes other powers: Elven Rage can switch to Dark Talion's version (floating spirit swords that get stuck and do nothing) or play plain, the stuck swords were undead Gondorian soldiers without bodies: the trainer now loads their bodies (except during story missions, which use their own character set), so the Gondorian Wights gear effect summons real soldiers. The trainer tries to keep Celebrimbor's Elven Rage; if rage still misbehaves, turn Raise the Dead OFF while you use Elven Rage.": "",
 "Prestige": "Prestigio",
 "Sword Prestige (Might gain)": "Prestigio de espada (poderío)",
 "Post-game Prestige ranks without finishing the story: the game's own PS_1Sword_Prestige_SKILL items, one per rank (max 100). +2.5% Might gain at rank 1, +35% at 50, +50% at 100.": "",
 "Dagger Prestige (crit damage)": "Prestigio de daga (daño crítico)",
 "+2.5% critical damage at rank 1, +35% at 50, +50% at 100.": "",
 "Bow Prestige (Focus on hit)": "Prestigio de arco (concentración)",
 "Focus gained on bow hits: 1 at rank 1, 14 at 50, 20 at 100.": "",
 "Armor Prestige (health on kill)": "Prestigio de armadura (salud)",
 "Health restored on kills: 2 at rank 1, 28 at 50, 40 at 100.": "",
 "Cape Prestige (mount attack/defence)": "Prestigio de capa (montura)",
 "Mount attack and defence: +3.75% at rank 1, +52.5% at 50, +75% at 100.": "",
 "Ring Prestige (Wrath gain)": "Prestigio de anillo (furia)",
 "Wrath / Elven Rage gain: +5% at rank 1, +70% at 50, +100% at 100.": "",
